### Phase 1: Canonical Data Model, Event Ontology & Provenance Schema

**Goal**: Establish a unified, immutable financial schema representing multi-source transactions (Bank, Payment Gateway, ERP/Invoices, Settlement Batches, Merchant/Customer Master) with full field-level lineage, transformation history, and taxonomy for decisions and diagnostic reasons.

#### ⚡ Flash Model Tasks (Boilerplate, Serialization & Schemas)
- Implement Pydantic v2 / dataclass models for `RawSourceRecord`, `CanonicalTransaction`, `PartyEntity`, `InvoiceRecord`, `PaymentEvent`, and `SettlementBatch`.
- Implement `FieldProvenance` tracking wrappers (`source_system`, `source_field`, `raw_value`, `normalized_value`, `transformation_fn`, `timestamp`).
- Define enumeration classes:
  - `DecisionLabel`: `MATCHED`, `EXCEPTION`, `UNCERTAIN`.
  - `ReasonCode`: `EXACT_MATCH`, `FEE_ADJUSTED_MATCH`, `SPLIT_PAYMENT_MATCH`, `DELAYED_SETTLEMENT`, `TIMING_DIFFERENCE`, `DUPLICATE_TRANSACTION`, `INVALID_REVERSAL`, `AMOUNT_MISMATCH`, `CURRENCY_MISMATCH`, `MISSING_SOURCE_RECORD`, `AMBIGUOUS_CANDIDATES`, `UNRESOLVED_CONTRADICTION`, `BUDGET_EXHAUSTED`.
- Write JSON/YAML schema validators and serialization/deserialization utilities.

#### 🧠 Pro Model Tasks (Financial Ontology & Lineage Architecture)
- Architect the multi-layered financial event ontology handling complex life-cycles: `AUTH` $\to$ `CAPTURE` $\to$ `FEE_DEDUCTION` $\to$ `SETTLEMENT` $\to$ `REFUND` / `CHARGEBACK` $\to$ `REVERSAL`.
- Formulate mathematical conservation laws for money across multi-entity splits:
  $$\sum \text{Gross Amount} = \text{Net Settlement} + \sum \text{Interchange/Gateway Fees} + \sum \text{Taxes}$$
- Design bidirectional graph schema mapping relationships (`INVOICE_TO_PAYMENT`, `PAYMENT_TO_SETTLEMENT`, `PARENT_TO_SPLIT`, `CHARGE_TO_REFUND`).

