### Phase 4: Multi-Stage Candidate Retrieval, Blocking & Entity Graph

**Goal**: Build a scalable retrieval pipeline that avoids $O(N^2)$ LLM comparisons by staging exact identifier blocking, lexical/fuzzy filtering, vector embeddings, and entity-graph neighborhood expansion.

#### ⚡ Flash Model Tasks (Vector Search & Index Plumbing)
- Integrate vector search library (FAISS, Chroma, or Qdrant) with pre-trained sentence transformers (e.g., `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` or `text-embedding-3-small`).
- Implement standard string distance functions (Levenshtein, Jaro-Winkler, Token Sort Ratio via `rapidfuzz`).
- Build fast in-memory inverted indexes and hash-based blocking tables (e.g. blocking on `(rounded_amount_bin, date_window, currency)`).
- Wire up NetworkX / rustworkx entity graph structures.

#### 🧠 Pro Model Tasks (Progressive Blocking & Graph Neighborhood Traversal)
- Design the **Progressive Entity Matching & Blocking Algorithm** balancing candidate reduction ratio ($RR > 99\%$) with pair completeness ($PC > 99.5\%$).
- Formulate the multi-attribute similarity scoring tensor:
  $$\mathbf{s} = [s_{\text{id}}, s_{\text{amount}}, s_{\text{date}}, s_{\text{text}}, s_{\text{graph}}, s_{\text{fee\_compat}}]$$
- Implement **Entity-Graph Neighborhood Expansion**: multi-hop traversal linking Customer $\to$ Invoices $\to$ Payments $\to$ Bank Deposits to resolve ambiguous references without leaking ground truth.

