### Phase 5: Deterministic Financial Rule Engine & 1-to-N Constraint Solver

**Goal**: Implement authoritative, versioned financial rules for arithmetic conservation, fee structures, date windows, currency compatibility, and an Integer Linear Programming (ILP) solver for one-to-many and split-payment matching.

#### ⚡ Flash Model Tasks (Rule Definitions & Solver Integration)
- Implement modular rule check classes inheriting from `BaseFinancialRule`:
  - `ExactAmountRule`, `DateWindowToleranceRule`, `CurrencyCompatibilityRule`, `DuplicateDetectionRule`.
- Build rule execution registry with version tagging (`v1.0.0`, `v1.1.0`) and execution metadata logging.
- Set up integration with optimization libraries (e.g. `PuLP`, `scipy.optimize`, or `ortools`).
- Write unit tests for individual rule evaluation passes and failures.

#### 🧠 Pro Model Tasks (Constraint Optimization & Invariant Engine)
- Architect the **Combinatorial 1-to-Many & Many-to-One Reconciliation Solver**:
  - Formulate the subset-sum / knapsack matching problem:
    $$\min \left| \text{TargetAmount} - \sum_{j=1}^M x_j \cdot (\text{Amount}_j - \text{Fee}_j) \right| \quad \text{subject to } x_j \in \{0, 1\}, \; \Delta t_j \le \tau$$
  - Implement penalty terms for temporal dispersion and entity mismatch.
- Formulate the **Deterministic Invariant Verification Engine**: Hard accounting assertions that can never be bypassed by LLM recommendations (e.g., negative net payouts, impossible exchange rates, double-counting already reconciled records).

