### Phase 8: Policy Verifier, Calibrated Decisioning & Audit Explainability

**Goal**: Implement the deterministic policy verifier that validates agent recommendations against accounting invariants, calculates calibrated risk scores, applies asymmetric decision thresholds, and generates auditor-ready explanation records.

#### ⚡ Flash Model Tasks (Report Generators, JSON Export & Review Queue Storage)
- Implement export formats for audit packages (PDF summary, JSON audit envelope, Markdown case report).
- Build the **Human-in-the-Loop Review Queue Service**: API endpoints to fetch pending cases, view evidence bundles, log human reviewer labels, and store review latency.
- Write unit tests verifying that malformed or uncited agent recommendations are caught and rejected.

#### 🧠 Pro Model Tasks (Asymmetric Calibration Mathematics & Verifier Engine)
- Formulate the **Calibrated Risk & Selective Prediction Engine**:
  - Train temperature scaling / Platt scaling or Isotonic Regression on validation log-odds to map raw model confidence to true posterior probabilities:
    $$P(\text{Match is Correct} \mid \mathbf{z}, \text{evidence})$$
  - Compute Expected Calibration Error (ECE) and Brier Score:
    $$\text{ECE} = \sum_{m=1}^M \frac{|B_m|}{N} \left| \text{acc}(B_m) - \text{conf}(B_m) \right|$$
- Formulate the **Asymmetric Cost-Weighted Decision Rule**:
  - Let $c_{\text{FP}} \gg c_{\text{U}} > c_{\text{FN}}$.
  - Accept `MATCHED` only if $\hat{P} \ge \tau_{\text{auto}} = 1 - \frac{c_{\text{U}}}{c_{\text{FP}}}$.
  - Route to `UNCERTAIN` when risk of false match exceeds threshold.
- Implement the **Deterministic Policy Verifier**:
  - Check that all cited record IDs exist in the evidence bundle.
  - Verify that claimed fee adjustments exactly match the deterministic rule output.
  - Veto and downgrade any `MATCHED` recommendation to `UNCERTAIN` if arithmetic invariance or uniqueness is violated.

