### Phase 10: Repeated-Seed Benchmarking, Statistical Evaluation & UI Dashboard

**Goal**: Execute repeated-seed benchmarking on held-out error templates ($N \ge 500$ transactions), compute statistical significance, cost-weighted utility, risk-coverage curves, and build an interactive investigation & review dashboard.

#### ⚡ Flash Model Tasks (Dashboard UI & Charting)
- Build an interactive Web Dashboard (Streamlit / Vanilla HTML+CSS+JS / FastAPI) featuring:
  - Batch execution view with real-time progress bars.
  - Interactive Case Investigation View: Evidence bundle viewer, graph relationship visualizer, agent tool-call timeline, and decision badge (`MATCHED`, `EXCEPTION`, `UNCERTAIN`).
  - Human Reviewer Modal: One-click approval, rejection, or manual re-assignment with reason logging.
  - Performance Summary Tab: Precision/Recall curves, confusion matrices, cost savings calculator.
- Implement CSV/JSON metric export scripts and plot generators (Matplotlib/Plotly).

#### 🧠 Pro Model Tasks (Statistical Benchmark Engine & Research Metric Suite)
- Implement statistical metric computation with 95% bootstrap confidence intervals across $\ge 5$ seeds:
  - *Core Metrics*: Precision, Recall, $F_1$, False-Match Rate (FMR), Exception Precision/Recall.
  - *Cause-Diagnosis Accuracy*: Multi-class accuracy on reason codes (`FEE_DIFF`, `TIMING_DIFF`, `SPLIT_PAYMENT`, `DUPLICATE`, `REVERSAL`).
  - *Cost-Weighted Objective Calculation*:
    $$\text{Utility} = B \cdot \text{TP} - c_{\text{FP}} \cdot \text{FP} - c_{\text{FN}} \cdot \text{FN} - c_{\text{U}} \cdot \text{Uncertain} - c_{\text{E}} \cdot \text{Unexplained}$$
    where $c_{\text{FP}} = \$500$, $c_{\text{FN}} = \$50$, $c_{\text{U}} = \$10$, $B = \$25$.
  - *Selective Prediction Metrics*: Risk-Coverage Curves (AURC - Area Under Risk-Coverage curve), Abstention Efficiency.
  - *Auditor Reproducibility & Citation Validity*: Automated checker verifying that $100\%$ of claims map to valid record IDs and exact arithmetic outputs.
- Write the final benchmark reporting suite that outputs breakdown tables by held-out scenario templates.

